-12-31 if any existed. But there are none in that test, and all existing tests that use `getInvoicesByDateRange` should pass fine with the inclusive range.\n\nLet me verify more carefully:\n\nTest \"returns invoices within a date range\" - range '2024-02-01' to '2024-03-15':\n- Matching dates: 2024-02-01, 2024-02-28, 2024-03-01 — 3 ✓ (was also 3 with exclusive end, since no invoice is on 2024-03-15... wait, there IS an invoice on 2024-03-15? Let me check.)\n- Seed dates: '2024-01-15', '2024-01-31', '2024-02-01', '2024-02-28', '2024-03-01', '2024-03-31', '2024-06-30'\n- Range: '2024-02-01' to '2024-03-15'\n- With `<=`: dates >= '2024-02-01' AND <= '2024-03-15': '2024-02-01', '2024-02-28', '2024-03-01' — 3 ✓ \n- With `<`: dates >= '2024-02-01' AND < '2024-03-16': '2024-02-01', '2024-02-28', '2024-03-01' — 3 ✓\n\nWait, the current query uses `AND date < ?`. So for the test, the end date is '2024-03-15'. With `<`, it's `date < '2024-03-15'`, meaning dates on 2024-03-15 are excluded. But none of the seed dates are exactly on 2024-03-15, so the result count is the same either way.\n\nLet me also check test \"cross-month boundary range\" - range '2024-01-15' to '2024-03-02':\n- With `<=`: dates >= '2024-01-15' AND <= '2024-03-02': '2024-01-15', '2024-01-31', '2024-02-01', '2024-02-28', '2024-03-01' — 5 ✓\n- With `<`: dates >= '2024-01-15' AND < '2024-03-02': same set — 5 ✓ (since no invoice on '2024-03-02')\n\nOK all good. Let me apply the fixes now.","signature":"9d49a4ff-5c05-4743-aafd-3327d4a13b0f"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2769,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":30464,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9042400b-3228-4a68-9f89-2a0fbc9d46c2","uuid":"f0e0ae6d-7740-4573-bd75-dfdec2ffa0e1"}
